 HISTORY                                                           301 1451
 -------                                                           301 1451
 This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction Physics   301 1451
 (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA. The         301 1451
 thermal scattering law data for crystalline graphite was          301 1451
 developed using ab initio lattice dynamics (AILD) [1-3]. The      301 1451
 coherent elastic cross sections were calculated based elastic     301 1451
 constants of a=2.4573 and c=6.700 angstroms from the values       301 1451
 present in NJOY2016. Distinct (Sd) effects are included in this   301 1451
 evaluation using directional information derived from the         301 1451
 crystalline graphite AILD structure [2-4]. Eight temperatures     301 1451
 are available in this library. The Full Law Analysis Scattering   301 1451
 System Hub (FLASSH) system was used to produce File 7 MT = 2, 4   301 1451
 data for graphite + Sd [4]. MAT=28 and ZA=128 are used for        301 1451
 crystalline graphite with distinct effects.                       301 1451
